        q: `  A 36-year-old woman has experienced increasing malaise for 3 weeks and has had a urine output of &#x3C;500 mL/day for the past 4 days. On examination, her blood pressure is 170/112 mm Hg, and she has peripheral edema. Urinalysis shows protein 1+ and blood 3+, but no glucose or ketones. Urine microscopic analysis shows RBCs and RBC casts. Her serum urea nitrogen level is 39 mg/dL, and creatinine is 4.3 mg/dL. Her serum complements C1q, C3, and C4 are decreased. A renal biopsy is performed, and immunofluorescence microscopy shows this pattern of staining with an antibody to C3.`,
