        q: `  A 45-year-old man has experienced increasing malaise, nausea, and reduced urine output for the past 3 days. On physical examination, he is afebrile and normotensive. Laboratory findings show a serum creatinine level of 7.5 mg/dL. Urinalysis shows hematuria, but no pyuria or glucosuria. A renal biopsy is done; the light microscopic image is shown in the figure. Which of the following additional laboratory studies is most likely to be useful for the classification and treatment of this disease?`,
