        q: `  A 21-year-old previously healthy man has noticed blood in his urine for the past 2 days. He reports no dysuria, frequency, or hesitancy of urination. On physical examination, there are no abnormal findings. Laboratory findings show a serum urea nitrogen level of 39 mg/dL and a creatinine level of 4.1 mg/dL. A renal biopsy specimen was obtained; the immunofluorescence staining pattern with an antibody against human IgG is shown below.`,
