        q: `  A 48-year-old man has had increased swelling in his extremities for 2 months. Physical examination shows generalized edema. A 24-hour urine collection yielded 4.1 g of protein. Laboratory studies now show a serum creatinine level of 4.5 mg/dL and a blood urea nitrogen level of 44 mg/dL. A renal biopsy was performed, and microscopic examination showed diffuse thickening of the basement membrane. Immunofluorescence staining with antibody to the C3 component of complement was positive in a granular pattern in the glomerular capillary loops. He did not respond to a course of corticosteroid therapy. Which of the following immunologic mechanisms is most likely responsible for the glomerular changes observed in the biopsy specimen?`,
