        q: `A 6-year-old girl has become increasingly lethargic over the past 2 weeks. On examination she has puffiness around the eyes. Her temperature is 36.9°C, and her blood pressure is 100/60 mm Hg. Laboratory findings show a serum creatinine level of 0.7 mg/dL, a urea nitrogen level of 12 mg/dL, and a cholesterol level of 217 mg/dL. Urinalysis shows 4+ proteinuria, lipiduria, and no blood or glucose. The 24-hour urine protein level is 3.8 g. The child’s condition improves after glucocorticoid therapy. Which of the following findings on electron microscopy is most likely to characterize this disease process?`,
