        q: `A 25-year-old male has experienced increasing malaise for the past 2 weeks. On physical examination, he has periorbital edema. Urine examination shows 3+ proteinuria, but no hematuria or glucosuria. The serum creatinine level is 2.3 mg/dL. He receives a course of corticosteroid therapy, but does not improve. A renal biopsy is performed and microscopic examination shows that approximately 50% of the glomeruli in the specimen are affected by the lesion shown below. Which of the following laboratory tests will most likely be abnormal in this case?`,
