        optionFeedback: [`Hemoptysis is a symptom (blood in the sputum) not associated with these renal abnormalities, although it may occur in patients who have anti-GBM antibodies that cross-react with the basement membrane of pulmonary alveoli (Goodpasture syndrome).`,`The histology is characteristic of benign nephrosclerosis, the disease associated with long-standing hypertension. The lesions are caused by narrowing of small arteries and arterioles, leading to chronic ischemic damage to glomeruli and tubules, and replacement of interstitium with scar tissue (fibrosis).`,`Lens dislocation is a manifestation of the genetic disease of connective tissues, Marfan syndrome, which is associated with aortic, cardiac and skeletal abnormalities but not renal disease.`,`pharyngitis and skin rash are signs of infection, (e.g. with streptococci) and may be antecedents of acute poststreptococcal GN, which presents with nephritis and glomerular lesions caused by immune complex deposition.`,`pharyngitis and skin rash are signs of infection, (e.g. with streptococci) and may be antecedents of acute poststreptococcal GN, which presents with nephritis and glomerular lesions caused by immune complex deposition.`,``],
