        ansText: `Rationale:- The history of frequent urination and fever suggests a urinary tract infection. The presence of white cells in the urine is diagnostic for pyelonephritis and the ultrasound findings are consistent with a chronic lesion (loss of renal parenchyma). The histology of the nephrectomy specimen is diagnostic of chronic pyelonephritis. Vesicoureteral reflux is a major predisposing condition because it allows bacteria from the lower urinary tract to travel retrograde to the kidneys.`,
        state: `notAnswered`,
