        ansText: `Rationale:- Chronic use of analgesics (especially phenacetin) is associated with renal disease called analgesic nephropathy. Patients present with progressive renal failure, often associated with hypertension, as in this case. The constitutional symptoms are likely related to renal failure. Papillary necrosis is a common pathologic manifestation of analgesic nephropathy. The disease stabilizes or improves if analgesics are discontinued.`,
        state: `notAnswered`,
        userAnswered: [],
