        q: `A 45-year-old man has had headaches, nausea, and vomiting that have worsened over the past 5 days. He has started “seeing spots” before his eyes and has experienced periods of mental confusion. On physical examination, his blood pressure is 270&#x2F;150 mm Hg. Urinalysis shows 1&#x2B; proteinuria; 2&#x2B; hematuria; and no glucose, ketones, or leukocytes. The serum urea nitrogen and creatinine levels are elevated. He dies 2 weeks later from a cerebral bleed. Which of the following histologic findings is most likely to be seen in this patient’s kidneys at autopsy?`,
